records.accounting_method:
Four-step integrated modeling workflow:
(1) SWAP economic model estimates per-region average annual cultivated acreage and permanent retirement to achieve SGMA-compliant water use;
(2) suitability-based land use change algorithm spatializes retirement at 1,080m pixel resolution across five driver-weighting scenarios;
(3) systematic conservation planning (spatial optimization via Prioritizr) identifies priority restoration areas minimizing agricultural opportunity cost while meeting habitat targets for five focal species;
(4) co-benefits assessment estimates soil carbon sequestration (LUCAS model, tracked to 2100) and excess nitrogen reduction (COMET-Farm, area-weighted by SWAP crop categories).

Spatial overlay framework linking GDE locations (DWR NCCAG dataset) to three ecosystem services:
(1) pollination: % of pollinator-dependent cropland within 1 km of GDE habitat;
(2) water quality regulation: GDE area between pollution sources and surface water bodies within 500m buffer;
(3) carbon sequestration: above- and below-ground carbon stocks within GDE polygons. Each service quantified by identifying production, beneficiaries, and spatial delivery overlap, then aggregated and normalized by SGMA groundwater basin.

records.data_sources:
California DWR Online State Well Completion Reports (OSWCR): 943,469 wells;
seasonal groundwater level measurements 1998–2017 (DWR);
2,027 reported domestic well failures from 2012–2016 drought (CA DWR/Governor's Office of Planning and Research);
ordinary kriging with Laurent correction for log-normal bias; Gaussian kernel density (bandwidth 433 m) for spatial calibration.
